contentText:
Depending on which way you care to split it, Sombr is either cool or hot. Choose a side.

The towering pop idol stopped by NBC&#8217;s The Tonight Show on Thursday, June 25 for the debut TV performance of his latest tune, &#8220;My Body Isn&#8217;t Ready.&#8221;

Wearing a body-hugging sparkly number, the New York native literally commanded the spotlight with his backing band in support.

Sombr (real name: Shane Boose) turned to his socials for some insights into his new song. &#8220;I hope this song can mean different things to different people,&#8221; he writes. &#8220;It can be taken as a metaphor. Or it can be taken literally as a description of how I have perceived my own body, for my whole life. I wanted to write about my struggle so that other people who may also be struggling know that they are not alone. You are beautiful, and I love you.&#8221;

The 20-year-old also hung out for a chat with the show&#8217;s host, Jimmy Fallon. Naturally, conversation swiftly turned to his career-affirming moment earlier this month when he inducted Taylor Swift into the Songwriters Hall of Fame , and performed a pair of her songs on the night.

&#8220;It was crazy,&#8221; he recounts. &#8220;It was really her night and she wanted me, out of all the people she could have asked, to perform two songs to help induct her.&#8221; Did she choose the songs? Nope. &#8220;So, basically I was like, &#8216;Taylor, what songs do you want me to sing? You know, this is your night.&#8217; And she was like, &#8216;no. You choose.'&#8221; That, he admits, &#8220;really put the pressure on.&#8221; He took a deep dive, came out with two songs, suggested them to her. Her response was, &#8220;perfect.&#8221;

On the night, he performed &#8220;Dear John&#8221; and &#8220;Cardigan.&#8221; Pressure off.

Swift has the highest of hopes for Sombr, and is almost jealous of his talents. That&#8217;s according to TayTay herself. Fallon took a moment to read for his audience some comments from the pop superstar, singing the praises of the precocious artist. &#8220;His writing is so exceptional, that it makes me actually envious. He&#8217;s going to be the top of my Spotify Wrapped this year, guaranteed. Sombr is the future.&#8221;

